Chapter: LadderBarWidthTest
  cites Works chapter MetalLadder
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The sink ladder's heartbeat reports progress as a bar, and on the ASUS the bar
 is the only thing that can separate a stage running slowly from a stage that
 died inside. Everything that can be got wrong in it is arithmetic, and none of
 that needs a framebuffer: a bar that saturates early, one that runs past the
 panel, one that divides before multiplying and reads zero across the whole
 first half.

 The row that matters most is `half of 2745998`. That is the real payload, and
 `w * done` there is 4,393,596,800, past 32 bits. A width computed in 32-bit
 arithmetic wraps to a small positive number and the bar jumps backwards in the
 middle of the fill, which on the glass reads as the write restarting.

Section: Test

  row : Text, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  row (tag) (w) (done) (total) =
    tag & "=" & show (ladder-bar-width w done total)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (row "zero-total" 1600 5 0)
    print-line-uni (row "negative-total" 1600 5 (0 - 3))
    print-line-uni (row "zero-done" 1600 0 100)
    print-line-uni (row "negative-done" 1600 (0 - 7) 100)
    print-line-uni (row "one-pct" 1600 1 100)
    print-line-uni (row "half" 1600 50 100)
    print-line-uni (row "all" 1600 100 100)
    print-line-uni (row "over" 1600 140 100)
    print-line-uni (row "narrow-panel" 640 50 100)
    print-line-uni (row "first-chunk" 1600 65536 2745998)
    print-line-uni (row "half-payload" 1600 1372999 2745998)
    print-line-uni (row "last-chunk" 1600 2703360 2745998)
    print-line-uni (row "whole-payload" 1600 2745998 2745998)
  end
